[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
claw2 is installed.

1. Copy the configuration and edit it:
     cp %%PREFIX%%/etc/claw2/claw2.yaml.sample %%PREFIX%%/etc/claw2/claw2.yaml
   The service makes the file its own when it starts: the web interface
   saves its settings into it.

2. Put the keys where the service reads them — as root, nobody else needs
   access (the service hands them to the gateway in its environment):
     cp %%PREFIX%%/etc/claw2/claw2.env.sample %%PREFIX%%/etc/claw2/claw2.env
     chmod 600 %%PREFIX%%/etc/claw2/claw2.env
         OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...                 (the model provider key)
         CLAW2_GATEWAY_API_KEY=<openssl rand -hex 24>

3. Enable and start the service:
     sysrc claw2_enable=YES
     service claw2 start

The interface is at http://<this host>:3000 and asks for the gateway key.
The log is /var/log/claw2.log.

Skills run in the soft sandbox (no Docker on FreeBSD): the Node.js
permission model plus the egress guard.
EOM
}
{ type: remove
  message: <<EOM
claw2 is removed. What was never the package's stays — for a reinstall, or
to delete by hand:
     %%PREFIX%%/etc/claw2/claw2.yaml, claw2.env   the configuration and the keys
     %%PREFIX%%/share/claw2                       the chats (data/) and the files
                                                 of the skills, if there are any
     /var/log/claw2.log, claw2_enable in /etc/rc.conf
     the account:  pw userdel claw2; pw groupdel claw2
EOM
}
]
